---
import CaseStudy from "../../components/CaseStudy.astro";
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Structuring complex"
  accent="B2B workflows."
  subtitle="Turning ambiguous operational requirements into a role-aware, record-centered prototype."
  role="Product Designer · Information Architecture, Prototyping, MVP Scoping"
  domain="B2B operations · Workflow design"
  timeline="Short discovery-to-prototype sprint"
  year="2026"
  tools="Collaborative mapping · AI-assisted prototyping · Design system"
  visual="fintech"
  iaComparison={true}
  sections={[
    {
      heading: "The context",
      paragraphs: [
        "The challenge was to make a complex, multi-step B2B service understandable to people working across distinct roles. Each role needed to move through a shared workflow while seeing the information and actions relevant to its responsibilities.",
        "The initial brief described process requirements but did not define how they should map to navigation or record context. I used it to shape a testable prototype and prioritize the essential journeys.",
      ],
    },
    {
      heading: "The information architecture challenge",
      paragraphs: [
        "An early prototype represented workflow steps as separate top-level destinations. This made it harder to understand which actions belonged to a specific record and what context was needed to complete them.",
        "The broader IA issue was that process steps and navigation destinations had been treated as interchangeable. Related tasks needed to stay connected to the record they concerned.",
      ],
    },
    {
      heading: "The design response",
      paragraphs: [
        "I regrouped related tasks around a selected record, while keeping workspace-level views and shared queues in the global navigation. I also made role-specific visibility an explicit part of the model.",
        "Using AI-assisted prototyping, I explored the hierarchy quickly, scoped a representative set of journeys, and documented open questions and trade-offs for future exploration.",
      ],
      items: [
        { title: "Global navigation", description: "Workspace overview, records, shared review queue, and performance views." },
        { title: "Contextual record", description: "Summary information stays with the selected record, alongside its files, activity, and decision history." },
        { title: "Role-aware model", description: "Visibility and permissions are made explicit so that role-specific behavior can be reviewed and tested." },
      ],
    },
    {
      heading: "Validation & product decisions",
      paragraphs: [
        "After establishing the hierarchy, I reviewed the prototype against the brief and identified assumptions that needed validation. I turned them into explicit product questions and design decisions.",
      ],
      items: [
        { title: "State clarity", description: "Make the status and next action for each task easy to understand." },
        { title: "Decision traceability", description: "Keep relevant history and rationale available as an item moves through a workflow." },
        { title: "Role boundaries", description: "Clarify who can view, edit, request, or approve each action." },
        { title: "Change management", description: "Represent significant changes in a way that preserves a clear record of what happened." },
      ],
    },
    {
      heading: "Stakeholder review",
      paragraphs: [
        "I shared the interactive prototype with cross-functional stakeholders and used the review to assess whether the structure made roles and task context understandable.",
        "The discussion also surfaced operational needs for further exploration, helping distinguish what the prototype addressed from questions that remained open.",
      ],
    },
    {
      heading: "What I took forward",
      paragraphs: [
        "AI-assisted prototyping can make it faster to explore complex workflows, but a coherent experience still depends on organizing requirements around people, roles, and the context of their work.",
        "The experience reinforced the value of validating the underlying structure before investing in detailed interface design, then carrying those decisions into a maintainable design and engineering handoff.",
      ],
    },
  ]}
/>
